00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:14.540
Philosopher.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.373
MARK MANDEL: Francesc
is looking on the air.

00:02:16.373 --> 00:02:18.190
So if you're not familiar
with Apache Kafka

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.590
while Francesc is
looking things up,

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.580
it's a messaging
system that is very

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.040
popular for a lot of people.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.820
Open source.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.569
We have Pub/Sub as a mini
messaging system here

00:02:28.569 --> 00:02:29.610
on Google Cloud Platform.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:32.960
But a lot of people do use Kafka
in and outside of Google Cloud

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.790
platform.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.747
FRANCESC CAMPOY: And
he wrote in German,

00:02:36.747 --> 00:02:38.580
but he was actually
from the Czech Republic,

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.340
from the
Austro-Hungarian Empire.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.340
MARK MANDEL: Important
information for everyone.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.423
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Very,
very important information.

00:02:44.423 --> 00:02:46.400
I like important information.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.322
Basically, what
we are announcing,

00:02:48.322 --> 00:02:50.030
which I think is really
cool, is the fact

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.960
that if you are a
Kafka user, you're

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.300
going to be able to integrate
very well with a bunch

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.180
of our technologies.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.250
So one of the ones that
I'm the most excited about

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.260
is the fact that you can
integrate with Cloud Pub/Sub.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.040
Both ways.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.300
So you can send from
Pub/Sub to Kafka and back.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.360
But then since you have that,
there's a bunch of other things

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:11.430
that also work.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.460
One of them is, you can use
it as a source for BigQuery.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.660
So you can stream into
BigQuery using Pub/Sub.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:23.290
You can also do
it now with Kafka.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:27.230
And finally, there's
also the possibility

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:30.800
of doing the same thing
streaming to Apache Beam

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:31.710
or Dataflow.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.260
Actually, Dataflow
and Apache Beam

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:34.560
are pretty much the same thing.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.268
MARK MANDEL: Yeah,
no, I really like this

00:03:36.268 --> 00:03:39.120
because if you want to put
Pub/Sub in your Workflow,

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:39.620
you can.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.244
So you can go Kafka
to Pub/Sub and then

00:03:41.244 --> 00:03:42.900
Pub/Sub to a number
of different things

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.402
like BigQuery or Dataflow.

00:03:44.402 --> 00:03:46.360
But if you don't want to
have another messaging

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.795
system within your system,
maybe for complexity's sake,

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.170
wanting to make
your life easier.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.700
You can go straight
from Kafka to Dataflow,

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.741
or straight from Kafka to
BigQuery, which I think

00:03:53.741 --> 00:03:54.960
that's really, really cool.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.876
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah,
it is very interesting,

00:03:56.876 --> 00:03:59.210
